Roast.pet Frontier Stack =E2=80=94 1 useful find

WAN 2.6 IMAGE-TO-VIDEO ON FAL =E2=80=94 TEST NOW

Source: https://fal.ai/models/wan/v2.6/image-to-video/api
Freshly surfaced production API documentation confirms Wan 2.6 I2V is
commercially usable on fal.

What changed / why relevant: Wan 2.6 I2V supports 720p and 1080p,
5/10/15-second clips, and multi-shot generation with intelligent scene
segmentation from a single starting image. This gives Roast.pet a
potentially useful middle tier between cheap single-shot animation and
expensive premium audiovisual generation: one canonical pet card can become
a structured multi-shot roast without separately generating and stitching
each shot.

Inputs/outputs: JPEG/JPG/PNG/BMP/WebP starting image (360=E2=80=932000 px, =
<=3D25MB)
+ motion prompt -> 720p/1080p video, selectable 5/10/15 sec.
API/install: fal hosted API via @fal-ai/client. Commercial use is
explicitly marked by fal.
Pricing: not sufficiently established from the authoritative API page in
this scan; benchmark actual billed cost rather than assume.
Privacy/self-hosting: this route is cloud-hosted. Do not send original
customer upload if the cleaned/canonical asset is sufficient.
Quality/latency constraint: multi-shot intelligence is the differentiator,
but it may introduce pet identity drift between shots; native
lip-sync/audio is not the reason to use this endpoint.
Exact Roast.pet use: canonical podium pet -> 10=E2=80=9315 sec multi-shot s=
equence:
setup close-up -> reaction/cutaway -> punchline hero shot. Deterministic
captions/audio can then be layered downstream.
Smallest test: 10 canonical pets, identical 10-sec three-beat prompt;
compare Wan 2.6 multi-shot against three separately generated 3=E2=80=934 s=
ec clips
stitched in the current pipeline. Score pet identity across cuts, shot
usefulness, edit labor, regeneration rate and billed cost.
Decision: TEST.

TOP 5 STACK CHANGES TO TEST NOW

   1. Wan 2.6 multi-shot versus separately generated/stiched roast shots.
   2. H3 Max Lip Sync + preselected multi-take TTS for exact joke delivery.
   3. Alphaveil/BiRefNet -> EdgeTAM -> ViTMatte local customer-photo
   preparation.
   4. Tsubaki.3/reference-image workflow for persistent canonical pet
   identity.
   5. Cheap-video -> automated identity/QC -> premium escalation routing.

CHEAPEST meaningful capability improvement: browser-local pet
cutout/refinement remains effectively $0 marginal inference.

BIGGEST CAPABILITY SHOCK THIS HOUR: not a new foundation-model leap; it is
a production-accessible multi-shot I2V path that could collapse Roast.pet=
=E2=80=99s
shot generation + stitching loop into one generation while retaining 1080p
output.

CONCRETE STACK SIMPLIFICATION TO TEST
Current conceptual path: canonical pet -> shot A + shot B + shot C ->
stitch/edit -> captions/audio.
Candidate: canonical pet -> Wan 2.6 10=E2=80=9315 sec multi-shot -> determi=
nistic
captions/audio.
Adopt only if identity survives scene cuts; otherwise separate shots remain
safer.

No padding: previously captured H3 Max Turbo/Lip Sync, Higgsfield,
Alphaveil, Tsubaki.3, Nari/Qwen3-TTS, HiDream and Vidu S2 were suppressed
as duplicates.

